2,4],[8,0,8,8,8,8,8,0,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[0,7,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,0,0,8,8,8,0,0,0],[0,7,2,0,4,0,0,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,8,1,4,0,0],[0,7,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,0,0,6,8,0,0,2,0],[7,7,7,0,0,0,0,4,8,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,0,7,7,7,7,7,7,0,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0],[0,7,6,6,9,9,0,4,4,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0],[0,7,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,0,7,0,8,0,0,2,0],[3,7,4,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,8,0,0,8,0,4,0,0],[0,7,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,6,0,0,8,0,0,0,0]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"## How the puzzle works\n\n**What the grids contain.** Each input has a background of 0. Scattered over it are many single-cell \"noise\" pixels and a few solid **3×3 squares**. There are two squares in pairs 1 and 4, one in pair 2, and three in pair 3. The test input has three: colour 4 centred at (3,7), colour 8 centred at (8,14), and colour 7 centred at (13,1).\n\n**What the output adds.** Compare pair 2, which has only one square: a colour‑4 block centred at (6,6). In the output, all of row 6 and all of column 6 are coloured 4, from border to border. That includes overwriting the noise pixels at (6,12) and (13,6). So every 3×3 square shoots a full-width horizontal line through its centre row and a full-height vertical line through its centre column, in its own colour.\n\n**Crossings.** Where there are several squares, the lines of different squares cross each other:\n- Pair 1: the row‑5 line (colour 2) meets the column‑4 line (colour 3) at (5,4). The output there is **0**. The same happens at (8,11).\n- Pair 3: every crossing between lines of different squares is 0, for example (3,4), (3,16), (10,12) and (15,12).\n- A square's own row and column cross at its own centre. That cell is inside the square and stays its colour.\n\n**Resulting rule.**\n1. Find every solid 3×3 square.\n2. For each square, paint its centre row and centre column across the whole grid in its colour.\n3. Any cell that lies on one square's row line and a *different* square's column line becomes 0.\n4. Re-stamp the squares so they stay intact.\n\n**Test input.** The three squares give rows 3, 8 and 13, and columns 7, 14 and 1. The six cross-square intersections become 0: (3,14), (3,1), (8,7), (8,1), (13,7) and (13,14). None of these falls inside a square, so the re-stamp in step 4 is only a safeguard.\n\n**Teaching stages emitted by the program:**\n1. One canvas per square after its two lines are drawn.\n2. A canvas after the crossings are cleared to 0.\n3. The final canvas after the squares are restored.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    blocks = []\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        if o[\"size\"] == 9 and y1 - y0 == 2 and x1 - x0 == 2:\n            blocks.append((y0 + 1, x0 + 1, o[\"colour\"], o[\"box\"]))\n    out = g.copy()\n    for cy, cx, c, _ in blocks:\n        out[cy, :] = c\n        out[:, cx] = c\n        emit(out, f\"Draw full row {cy} and column {cx} in colour {c} through the centre of the 3x3 square.\")\n    for i, (cy, _, _, _) in enumerate(blocks):\n        for j, (_, cx, _, _) in enumerate(blocks):\n            if i != j:\n                out[cy, cx] = bg\n    emit(out, \"Clear every crossing between lines of different squares to background.\")\n    for _, _, c, (y0, x0, y1, x1) in blocks:\n        out[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1] = c\n    emit(out, \"Restore the 3x3 squares themselves; final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Re-stamp the squares so they stay intact."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"None of these falls inside a square, so the re-stamp in step 4 is only a safeguard."}],"repair":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The final canvas after the squares are restored."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Restore the 3x3 squares themselves; final grid."}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So every 3×3 square shoots a full-width horizontal line through its centre row and a full-height vertical line through its centre column, in its own colour."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"None of these falls inside a square, so the re-stamp in step 4 is only a safeguard."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"f6c5339af8f32a9d822786a368300b8907f3469acfe0e19b0702b75fc4e710af","task_sha256":"cd5ca98d05dacf1a78f4b234e11da05fbc42c588299905eae5375da8a3a29555","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
